    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0661" n="593" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/3312c</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 5, 1917</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: The British Ambassador
                    called upon Mr. Phillips<anchor n="92a" xml:id="d561-f1"/> this morning and
                    asked that you be advised privately that he had received a message from the Duke
                    of Devonshire, Governor-General of Canada, expressing, not only on his own
                    behalf but on behalf of both parties and the people of Canada, the intensity of
                    their feeling of admiration for the course which you have taken.</p>
                <p>Apparently it is the policy of the British Government to suppress to a
                    considerable extent the press reports of the tremendous enthusiasm <pb
                        facs="0662" n="594" xml:id="pg594"/> in the British Empire, not only in
                    Government circles but in all classes of society including the labor element,
                    fearing that the outburst of enthusiasm, which has in fact occurred, if
                    advertised too much, might not be desirable from the point of view of this
                    country. Sir Cecil Spring Rice therefore has informed the Duke of Devonshire
                    that his message to you is being communicated unofficially through me.</p>
                <p>With assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
